    echo "root: <repo> stands for the repository's top level (inside <home>, so scrubbed first); scripts/counting.sh is sourced from it by this log, the gate log ($GATE_LOG) is read for the binary's hash, the template files, crates/emend/src/cells.rs, crates/emend/src/package.rs, crates/emend/src/styles/elements.rs, crates/emend/src/package/tests/comments/rich.rs and $SPEC are read from it by git show, and $SPEC's working file is hashed and read in it; nothing in it is run: the binary under test is the gate's, copied into <tree>/bin and run from there"
